  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "A Chalcolithic cemetery located at modern Polg\u00e1r, Hungary, with at least 156 graves. This site is the typesite for the Tiszapolg\u00e1r or Tiszapolg\u00e1r-Rom\u00e2ne\u015fti culture, an Eneolithic archaeological culture. This archaeological culture has been identified on the Great Hungarian Plain and elsewhere in eastern, central Europe. It dates ca. 4500-4000 BCE.",
